    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for broadcasting a tensor along a new dimension. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradBroadcast" kindref="compound">GradBroadcast</ref> class represents the broadcasting operation in the computational graph, computing gradients for expanding a tensor by adding a new dimension and replicating the tensor&apos;s values along that dimension. For the operation where tensor <formula id="12">$A$</formula> of shape <formula id="16">$(d_1, \ldots, d_n)$</formula> is broadcast to tensor <formula id="17">$C$</formula> of shape  <formula id="18">$(d_1, \ldots, d_{pos}, N, d_{pos+1},
\ldots, d_n)$</formula> at position <formula id="19">$pos$</formula>, the gradient computation follows from:    <formula id="20">\[    \frac{\partial C_{i_1,\ldots,i_{pos},j,i_{pos+1},\ldots,i_n}}{\partial
A_{i_1,\ldots,i_n}} = 1
\]</formula> for all <formula id="21">$j$</formula>.</para>
<para>During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="15">$\frac{\partial
L}{\partial C}$</formula> (which has the broadcast dimension) must be summed along the broadcast dimension to match the shape of the input tensor according to the chain rule:    <formula id="22">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A_{i_1,\ldots,i_n}} = \sum_{j}
\frac{\partial L}{\partial C_{i_1,\ldots,i_{pos},j,i_{pos+1},\ldots,i_n}}
\]</formula></para>
<para>The backward pass performs a sum reduction along the broadcast dimension, effectively gathering gradients from all the replicated copies back to the original tensor. This operation is the inverse of the forward broadcasting.</para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves the input tensor from the forward pass to determine the shape for gradient reduction, and stores the position of the broadcast dimension.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradReductionSum" kindref="compound">GradReductionSum</ref> for the gradient function for sum reduction along a dimension. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
